# Quality Gates

Lint and test failures are defects. Fix on the branch; do not bypass hooks.

## Dogfooding

ShipGate is a quality-control repo; it must pass its own gates. No carve-outs for "mature" or legacy code.

| Principle | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| Full codebase | Built-in gates and every suite check (ruff, ty, radon, semgrep, bandit, policy gates, etc.) apply to the **entire** codebase |
| No grandfathering | Do not relax thresholds, narrow scopes, or skip checks for existing code — fix violations |
| Allowlists | `.shipgate/allowlists/` entries require an exceptional, documented reason; prefer code fixes over exemptions |

## Commands

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `pytest tests/unit -q` | Default deterministic suite |
| `pytest -m integration` | External tools, network, pip install |
| `ruff check src tests` | Lint |
| `ruff format --check src tests` | Format check |

## Rules

- Never use `git commit --no-verify` or `SKIP=...`.
- Default tests must not require external tool binaries.
- Run the smallest relevant command after each risky change.
- Before claiming done, run fresh commands and report actual results.
